.TH geectl-pull-request-submit 1  "geectl-pull-request-submit 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-submit \- File a submission from the working copy in the current directory: an OBS submit request from an OBS\-native checkout, a Gitea pull request from a git\-backed one. The checkout\*(Aqs backend decides; the other arm\*(Aqs flags are refused, except the submission text: `\-\-title`/`\-\-body` work on both arms, and on OBS they compose `\-\-description` (the title as the headline, the body after a blank line). Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request submit\fR [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-changes\-entry\fR] [\fB\-\-cve\fR] [\fB\-\-without\-cleanup\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-head\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-body\fR] [\fB\-\-draft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
File a submission from the working copy in the current directory: an OBS submit request from an OBS\-native checkout, a Gitea pull request from a git\-backed one. The checkout\*(Aqs backend decides; the other arm\*(Aqs flags are refused, except the submission text: `\-\-title`/`\-\-body` work on both arms, and on OBS they compose `\-\-description` (the title as the headline, the body after a blank line). Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The project the request targets: the devel project, or openSUSE:Factory when the source is the recorded devel project and package. OBS only; required there
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The package in the target project. OBS only; the checkout package when unset
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The request description: one headline, then `\- ` lines for staging, needs, and rebuilds. OBS only; required there unless `\-\-title` is given (the two are spellings of the same text — pass one, not both). Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a description may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-changes\-entry\fR \fI<CHANGES_ENTRY>\fR
The one `.changes` entry for this submission. It must name every CVE passed with `\-\-cve`. OBS only; required there. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a `.changes` entry starts with `\- `
.TP
\fB\-\-cve\fR \fI<CVE>\fR
A CVE this submission claims to fix. Repeatable; each one must be named in `\-\-changes\-entry`. OBS only
.TP
\fB\-\-without\-cleanup\fR
Keep the source branch on accept instead of deleting it (cleanup is the default). OBS only
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
The repo to open the pull request in (`owner/repo`). Gitea only; the parent of the checkout\*(Aqs origin remote (the fork\*(Aqs parent, never the fork) when unset
.TP
\fB\-\-head\fR \fI<HEAD>\fR
The branch the change comes from. Gitea only; the checkout\*(Aqs current branch when unset
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BASE>\fR
The branch the pull request targets. Gitea only; the branch the checkout tracks (its scmsync branch) when unset, else the target repo\*(Aqs default branch. The `factory` branch does not take pull requests
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
The submission title. On Gitea the pull request title, required there; on OBS the headline of the request description, in place of `\-\-description`. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally
.TP
\fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
The submission body. On Gitea the pull request body; on OBS the text after the headline in the request description, in place of `\-\-description` together with `\-\-title`. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: the body may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-draft\fR
Open the pull request as a draft. Gitea only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
